The token sequence construction, question rendering, confidence calculation,
presets, email utilities and language router are adapted from Laya.
The neural network is reimplemented using Apple's MLX, following Laya's
DecisionModel and the ModernBERT architecture in Hugging Face Transformers.
Model weights are downloaded separately from Convai Innovations on Hugging Face;
they are not included in this repository.

The T-Rex demo (laya_mlx/trex) is a Python port of the offline dinosaur game in Chromium
(components/neterror/resources/dino_game, commit 0fd1c14b0bc9c294cf49a74cdafe9be1a7e7330a).
Its sprite sheets and sounds are copied from Chromium. Copyright The Chromium Authors,
BSD 3-Clause; see laya_mlx/trex/assets/LICENSE.chromium.

The live feed probe (social/live) adapts four browser mechanisms from jev-browser:
https://github.com/Ying-Kai-Liao/jev-browser
Copyright 2026 Ying-Kai Liao. Licensed under MIT.
The persistent-context launch, settle-by-mutation-timestamp detection with its
self-mutation and stale-request guards, and the overlay injection recipe are adapted
from its session driver.

